	(text "NFC (ST25DV04KC, DS13519 Rev 2)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ba7cdc21-b0df-55da-97aa-499d0b5befad"))
	(text "ST25DV04K is NRND; the KC version replaces it. UFDFPN8 (2x3 mm) is the smallest package ordered\nfor the 04KC and has the open-drain GPO. Its exposed pad must be left floating (symbol pin 9 is NC).\nVCC comes from MCU PB0 only while awake: standby with VCC on is 72-100 uA (LPD needs the 12-pin package).\nGPO: open drain, active low (level or low pulse). Works from RF power alone with VCC off (DS13519\nFigure 7), so a phone tap wakes the MCU on PA8 / EXTI8. Default GPO mode is RF field change.\nPull-up R14 to always-on VBAT, 1M (> 4.7k required): no current while GPO is high-Z.\nI2C with VCC off: DS13519 gives leakage (0.1 uA max) only in standby; the I/O absolute maximum is\n-0.5 to 6.5 V independent of VCC, which points to no clamp to VCC. Check on the first board; fallback:\nmove R6/R7 (RTC sheet) to NFC_VCC and raise PB0 before any I2C transfer.\nCoil: L = 1/(w^2 C) = 4.8 uH for 28.5 pF (4.4 uH with ~3 pF parasitic). 7-8 turns, 39 mm OD,\n0.15/0.15 mm on F.Cu (r 17.25-19.5 mm), underpass on B.Cu. The CR2032 and holder lower L (tune upward)\nand cut Q. 8 turns is ~5.5 uH free air, so with the cell it should land at or below 4.8 uH (f >= 13.56 MHz);\nC22 then pulls f down after a VNA check. If it measures low, drop to 7 turns." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 147.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9f0b0d96-afd6-5e49-b105-3bc33b55f691"))
